    <briefdescription>
<para>Inspection queries that read a series&apos; own buffer whose records are ordered along one axis. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput>order</computeroutput> argument names the axis whose coordinates are finite and non-decreasing. Positions along it are found by binary search, so no index is built and appended records are visible immediately. Per-block extents and Y statistics are cached lazily to answer large region summaries and to prune nearest-point searches. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
